        <briefdescription>
<para>Retrieve the node matching a function declaration (using mangled name to resolve across translation units) </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Double checks that the Call <ref refid="classGraph" kindref="compound">Graph</ref> has the function.</para><para><ref refid="classCallGraphBuilder_1ab6f61c25d29cdf9e93276c02e0ee2b59" kindref="member">CallGraphBuilder::getGraphNodeFor</ref></para><para>This double checks for a call graph node. If multiple files are input on the command line firstNondefiningDeclartion may not be unique. (As expected) So we can double check on the name. This is useful only outside the <ref refid="classCallGraph" kindref="compound">CallGraph</ref>, if the <ref refid="classCallGraph" kindref="compound">CallGraph</ref> is fully constructed, and we need a particular node from it.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
